      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: This scalar tail has a logic error. Pointer A and B were not advanced during the SIMD loop (which used A + i), but here you are using A[0] and A[1] while incrementing the pointers. This means if the SIMD loop processed 16 samples (i\u003d16), this tail will incorrectly re-process data starting from A[0] instead of A[16].\n\nYou should either advance the pointers before the loop:\nA +\u003d i; B +\u003d i;\nor use the index:\nA[i + 0], A[i + 1]... (and don\u0027t increment A/B in the loop).\n\nNote that SharpYuvFilterRow32_AVX2 correctly uses the index approach.",
